{"id":"rel.wave2.batch41.01","from_formulation":"form.wave2.alternative39.borel-sigma-algebra-topological","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.topological-space","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"topological space","editorial_reason":"The Borel sigma-algebra is generated by the open sets of the ambient topological space (X,τ), so the topology is a genuine prerequisite; this does not identify an arbitrary sigma-algebra with a Borel sigma-algebra.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ABorel_Sigma-Algebra","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ATopological_Space","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_source_mathematical_comparison_2026_10_20","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch41.02","from_formulation":"form.wave2.alternative39.borel-sigma-algebra-topological","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.sigma-algebra","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"sigma-algebra","editorial_reason":"The Borel construction takes the smallest sigma-algebra containing τ, hence requires the sigma-algebra axioms before imposing the topological generation condition.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ABorel_Sigma-Algebra","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASigma_Algebra","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_source_mathematical_comparison_2026_10_20","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch41.03","from_formulation":"form.wave2.alternative39.boolean-ring-unital","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.associative-ring-identity-optional","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"associative ring R","editorial_reason":"Boolean idempotence x²=x is an extra law on the underlying associative ring. The independently sourced ring axioms supply addition, multiplication and distributivity; the required unit remains an explicit further hypothesis.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ABoolean_Ring","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_%28Abstract_Algebra%29","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_source_mathematical_comparison_2026_10_20","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch41.04","from_formulation":"form.wave2.alternative39.boolean-ring-nonunital","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.associative-ring-identity-optional","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"associative ring R","editorial_reason":"The possibly nonunital Boolean-ring convention is exactly an associative ring with idempotent multiplication for every element. A general associative ring with optional identity is the correct prerequisite and does not silently insert unity.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ABoolean_Ring","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_%28Abstract_Algebra%29","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_source_mathematical_comparison_2026_10_20","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch41.05","from_formulation":"form.wave2.alternative39.bipartite-undirected","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.subset-nonstrict","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"subsets A,B⊆V","editorial_reason":"The bipartition condition quantifies over disjoint subsets A and B of the vertex set V. Non-strict subset inclusion is a mathematical prerequisite; the graph/edge structure still needs separate independent sourcing.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ABipartite_Graph","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubset","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_source_mathematical_comparison_2026_10_20","human_verified":false}
